cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GovTrade in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "GovTrade: Learned Adaptive Governance in Multi-Agent Financial Systems"
authors:
  - family-names: Sarkar
    given-names: Arka
    email: arkasarkar1507@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/ARKAISW/GovTrade"
abstract: >
  GovTrade is an open benchmark environment for studying learned financial governance.
  It models institutional oversight as a three-agent Dec-POMDP and documents
  Cooperative Strangulation, a MARL failure mode where supervisory agents
  converge to a permanent shutdown policy, achieving zero constraint violations
  at the cost of complete portfolio inactivity.
keywords:
  - multi-agent reinforcement learning
  - financial governance
  - AI safety
  - Dec-POMDP
  - cooperative strangulation
  - benchmark
license: MIT
year: 2026
